 "seed": 25,
 "notes": "1907 four-storey (read as three window storeys over a low sloping brick base on the Hyde fall) red common-bond brick warehouse. 20 bays, tall segmental-arched windows in dark frames, brick surround arches, string courses between storeys, pilaster-like piers every few bays, stepped parapet with a deeper cornice. Entry door near the right end. Sign and downpipes not modelled. Three window rows read over a low brick plinth, so the stack is now a 1.9 m plinth (small arched vents) plus three 3.2 m window storeys (4 levels). White cornice/string course replaced by brick-toned trim (the real parapet is brick); round iron anchor plates added between the storeys; pale downpipes added. Windows keep segmental arches and dark frames on the front; the square-headed windows in the 3/4 view are the short rear return (not a street face). Skipped: raised centre parapet plaque and the corbelled brick band (no key). Skipped as already done or unsupported: a 4th window storey (3 window rows over a plinth; 4 levels built), white cornice (already brick), semicircular heads (heads are segmental), tall arched ground doors (one door only). Tint lift (2026-10-02): paint tints lifted toward the sunlit paint (t' = 1-(1-t)k); brick tints converted to target / kit colour. Now brick-buff with a warm tint. Wall back to brick-common-bond with a near-neutral tint (brick-buff plus pink tint rendered lavender), frames dark green-black, hand.py adds three brick pilaster strips at the downpipe positions. Not added: hotel sign panel (names forbidden). Budget: build was over the 60000 exterior triangle cap, so the soldier-arch surrounds on upper windows were dropped to fit; segmental heads kept.",
